From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:54:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(delegation): adopt owner-claimed units without
 replacing ledger [daveey]

Problem: live child work correctly vetoes update checkpointing; parent parking alone
cannot preserve the child. The existing async dispatch always creates/replaces its
unit row, so it cannot register already-claimed work under its original identity.
Why 1: continue creates a new delegation ID rather than reusing completion custody.
Why 2: capacity, ledger insert, lease, retirement, monitor and finalization shared one
new-dispatch-only path (tools/async_delegation.py _dispatch_admitted).
Root (happened): no scheduling seam for an owner-claimed durable running unit.
Root (not caught): prior pause fixes were accepted on clean windows without a live
child/reservation precondition; no restart-with-child contract was exercised.
Recurrence: hub due-to-apply remained 570s/1015s after earlier pause guards;
this is only authorized slice2a, not a claim those failures are repaired.

Add adopt_unit for a row already owned by this exact process incarnation. Recheck
unchanged durable custody under the registry lock; reject duplicates, terminal or
settled rows. Use common admitted scheduling without resetting ledger/delivery
state; retain the row on executor/lease/submit failure. Restore original routing,
time, transcripts, slot and partial children, joining them through the original
one-shot finalizer. Persist slot_key for new units; legacy rows use an independent
conservative slot. No parked state, ownership transfer, crash retry, new config or
update-admission relaxation. Child receipt CAS/resume and real SIGKILL-after-park
proof are deliberately separate slice2b; no partial park implementation here.

Proof: canonical adoption RED13 missing-module failures; final focused21 passed.
155 consumer files:3132 passed,0 failed,5 platform skips.20/20 mutants killed with
green baseline (identity,state,delivery,stale/duplicate,partial,slot,lease,reservation,
capacity,closed-session,monitor,ledger preservation). Full scripts/check21 checks OK.
Live check: none for this slice; installed timeline instrumentation is separate.
Undo: reviewed revert; this change cannot produce parked rows.
